{"role":"assistant","content":"Done. All six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` are implemented via `Analytics.capture`, and the summary is in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**`lib/screens/registration_screen.dart`**\n- `registration_email_started` / `registration_phone_started` — fire once per visit on the first keystroke, gated by `_emailInputFired` / `_phoneInputFired` flags (registration_screen.dart:44, registration_screen.dart:57)\n- `loan_amount_changed` — fires in `onChangeEnd` once per drag, only if the value actually changed since `onChangeStart`, with `{'amount': int}` (registration_screen.dart:75)\n- `terms_accepted` — fires only on the false → true checkbox transition (registration_screen.dart:88)\n- `registration_continue_tapped` — fires in the Continue button with `{'amount': int, 'terms': bool}` before navigating (registration_screen.dart:100)\n\n**`lib/screens/offer_screen.dart`**\n- `offers_scrolled` — a `NotificationListener<ScrollEndNotification>` wraps the offers list and sends `{'offset': double}` once per scroll gesture (offer_screen.dart:32)\n\nFrom the colleague's note, the parts that applied: once-per-visit flags for text fields, slider capture in `onChangeEnd`, scroll capture on `ScrollEndNotification`, and keeping event names/properties unchanged. I added one adaptation — the slider event only fires when the value truly moved (the spec says \"user moved the slider\"). Ignored: focus-lost/final-value capture (no event needs it, and PII is forbidden) and the note's diagnostic/verification steps, since this was a fresh implementation rather than a fix for an existing event storm. Full rationale is in `ANSWER.md`.\n\nOne caveat: I could not run `flutter analyze` — the sandbox blocks executing the Flutter SDK binaries — so verification was a careful manual review of both files. Worth running the analyzer on a machine where the SDK can execute."}
